      "output": "# Static review — Umber test report vs spec\n\n**Nature of this review:** I read the supplied report and spec only. I did **not** run `awwo-check-page`, `window.awwoSelfTest()`, or any browser; I did not verify the SHA-256. All counts below are what the report *states*; I confirmed nothing myself. Static review and actual execution are kept strictly separate.\n\n## Acceptance checks by number\nThe report gives aggregates (**61 of 63 passed, 20/20 planted caught, 0 page errors, non-blank, 349 colours**) but prints **no per-number table** for spec §10 tests 1–30, and uses test *names* that don't map cleanly to the numbers. So:\n- **Shown PASSING by name (map to §10 numbers):** `demo size & count` → **1**; `demo names` → **2**; `demo not checker & size` → **3**; `files demo >=8 & 2 adj`, `view: fit centres` → **11**-ish; `reordering rows`, `panel redrawn` → **25**-ish. The two selection fixes and the paint fix are named (`subtract removes overlap`, `wand tol0`, `paint:dab area`) but not tied to numbers.\n- **Shown FAILING:** `panels: bring forward moves layer up` → **24** (report argues +1 behaviour is correct and the test's `=== 1` expectation conflicts with a sibling test; left unfixed). `invert twice restores every pixel` → relates to **21** (fails in the test's own `new ImageData(w*h)` setup, never reaching `adjust.apply`; left unfixed).\n- **Not individually shown — not actually run per number:** **4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 22, 23, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30.** Folded into the 61 total but no per-number result given.\n\nAlso note: the report counts **63** self-tests and **20** planted failures, while spec §10 lists **30** tests and §11 lists only **P1–P10**. The mapping and this count discrepancy are **not actually shown**.\n\n## Planted failures caught\nReport states **20 of 20** rejected (both runs). It does not name any P1–P10 or map them to tests, so *which* planted failures were caught is **not actually shown** — only the count.\n\n## What the fixes changed (as reported)\nFour local edits: (1) **compositor** — exclude masked layers from the native fast path so the per-pixel path honours the mask (`mask hides`). (2) **selection** — `oOpt(tool,name)` so marquee reads its own `mode`/`feather`. (3) **selection** — wand reads its own `tolerance`/`contiguous`/`sample`; lasso updated too. (4) **paint** — keep the dab's outer stop solid at hardness 100 (`paint:dab area`).\n\n## Spec parts no check shows coverage for\nPer this report: 23 of 27 blend modes; non-sep hue/sat/color/luminosity, dissolve; 10 of 12 adjustments, most of 11 filters; transform, cut/copy/paste, clone/gradient/shape/type/eyedropper/hand/zoom; crop/trim, image rotate/flip/resize; feather/grow/colour-range; save/load (§8); export; palette-run (28), shortcuts, layout/look (§6). **Verdict: FAIL (61/63).**",
